<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕtrēta</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετρητής</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an Athenian measure
				for liquids, containing</i> 12 congii (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόες</span>) <i>and</i> 144 <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοτύλαι</span> (3/4 <i>of the
				Attic medimnus, about</i> 9 <i>gallons
			English</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">picis liquidae metreta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 22, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se vendidisse navem, metretas quae trecentas
					tolleret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. prol. 75</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a tun, cask,
			jar</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum si in metretam novam inditurus eris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 100</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hispanae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					5, 16, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olivariae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hic tignum capiti incutit, ille metretam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 246</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
